s":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/74091","html_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74091","diff_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74091.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/74091.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-05T09:05:05Z"},"body":"## Why\r\n\r\nA core Dag-serialization schema change shipped recently with the Go SDK's vendored copy left behind, and nothing caught it: the Go and Java sync hooks were manual-only, and the check that runs on every commit (`check-go-sdk-generated-drift`) watches the *vendored copies*, not the Python source, so it never saw the schema change at all. The same class of drift already caused a two-release-old bug in the Go SDK's generated models (#73954).\r\n\r\n## What\r\n\r\n- `sync-go-sdk-schemas` and `sync-java-sdk-dag-schema` now run on every commit (dropping `stages: ['manual']`), and are both triggered by the Python schema source itself, not just the vendored copy — matching how `sync-ts-sdk-dag-schema` already worked. Each refreshes the vendored copy and fails when it had to, so the refresh gets reviewed and committed rather than shipping unnoticed.\r\n- `check-go-sdk-generated-drift`'s trigger now also includes the Python schema sources, so it fires in the same commit as the sync hook above and catches generated Go code that still needs regenerating from the freshly-synced copy.\r\n- Java's underlying Gradle task (`SyncDagSchemaTask`) gains a `failOnRefresh` flag, off by default. `generateDagDsl`'s existing dependency keeps the flag off, so an ordinary in-repo build still refreshes a schema a developer is actively editing without breaking. The prek hook now calls a second task instance (`checkDagSchemaSync`) with the flag on.\r\n\r\n## How I verified it\r\n\r\nRan each hook directly with a deliberately corrupted vendored copy and confirmed it refreshes the file and fails:\r\n- `prek run sync-java-sdk-dag-schema --files airflow-core/src/airflow/serialization/schema.json`\r\n- `prek run sync-go-sdk-schemas --files airflow-core/src/airflow/serialization/schema.json`\r\n- `prek run check-go-sdk-generated-drift --files airflow-core/src/airflow/serialization/schema.json`\r\n\r\nAlso confirmed `./java-sdk/gradlew :sdk:generateDagDsl` still refreshes silently and succeeds (no regression to the normal in-repo build), while `:sdk:checkDagSchemaSync` fails on the same drift.\r\n\r\nNo newsfragment: CI/build tooling only, no user-facing behavior change.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\r\n\r\n- [X] Yes — Claude Code (Opus 4.7)\r\n\r\nGenerated-by: Claude Code (Opus 4.7) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/74091/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/74091/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":32340107024,"node_id":"REFE_lADOAgUK288AAAABUI0p488AAAAHh57fEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/events/32340107024","actor":{"login":"pierrejeambrun","id":14861206,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODYxMjA2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14861206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun","html_url":"https://github.com/pierrejeambrun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pierrejeambrun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/user